# One self-attention block from a real, open-source pretrained
# Transformer: google/vit-base-patch16-224-in21k (Vision Transformer,
# HuggingFace), extracted and validated against genuine ImageNet-21k-
# trained weights, not a toy-trained model.
#
# This is the "extract one attention block" strategy: rather than
# compiling the whole ViT model (which needs operators Tensora does
# not have -- patch-embedding conv, layernorm, GELU; to be considered
# in future),
# tools/models/prepare_vit_attention_demo.py runs a real photograph
# through the real HuggingFace model up to one encoder layer's
# self-attention block, captures that block's real input hidden state
# and its real output, and exports the block's own Q/K/V/output-
# projection weights (all genuine pretrained parameters -- no
# retraining, no synthetic weights). Tensora then recomputes that one
# block from the same input and the same weights, and the demo checks
# the two outputs agree. The prep script extracts the LAST encoder
# layer (layer index 11 of 12): later layers give a more legible,
# subject-focused attention pattern than layer 0 for the visualization
# part of the demo; the numerical equivalence check (make
# demo-vit-attention) holds for any layer.
#
# Shapes match ViT-Base exactly: hidden_size=768, num_attention_heads=
# 12, head_dim=64 (12*64=768), sequence length 197 (196 16x16 patches
# from a 224x224 image, plus one [CLS] token).
#
# The `head` axis is on Q/K/V/output-projection from the start: since
# general reshape is not lowered, no reshape is used to split/merge
# it -- batched matmul/transpose/sum handle the per-head math
# directly. `bq`/`bk`/`bv` carry ViT's real per-head
# Q/K/V bias (`qkv_bias=True` in the ViT config); `bo` is the real
# output-projection bias. Scale = 1/sqrt(64), the model's own value.
input  Xq: Tensor[b=1, head=1, qseq=197, d=768]
input  Xk: Tensor[b=1, head=1, kseq=197, d=768]
weight Wq: Tensor[b=1, head=12, d=768, dk=64]
weight bq: Tensor[head=12, qseq=1, dk=64]
weight Wk: Tensor[b=1, head=12, d=768, dk=64]
weight bk: Tensor[head=12, kseq=1, dk=64]
weight Wv: Tensor[b=1, head=12, d=768, dv=64]
weight bv: Tensor[head=12, kseq=1, dv=64]
weight Wo: Tensor[b=1, head=12, dv=64, d=768]
weight bo: Tensor[d=768]

graph vit_attn_block {
    Qp     = Xq @ Wq
    Q      = Qp + bq
    Kp     = Xk @ Wk
    K      = Kp + bk
    Vp     = Xk @ Wv
    V      = Vp + bv
    Kt     = transpose(K, perm=[0, 1, 3, 2])
    scores = Q @ Kt
    scaled = scores * 0.125
    A      = softmax(scaled, axis=kseq)
    ctx    = A @ V
    proj   = ctx @ Wo
    merged = sum(proj, axis=head)
    out    = merged + bo
    return out
}
